WEBVTT

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.400
Right.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:09.150
Down.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.150
Left.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.270
Upper right.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.700
Upper left.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.170
Down.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.060
Right.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:17.900
Lower right.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:18.370
Left.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.430
Wow.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.640
1.2 vision without glasses...

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.330
That's not the issue!

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.620
Okay, let's try this.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.730
A butterfly man?

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.130
No. Mothman.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.030
Cobra!

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.460
No. Tsuchinoko.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.130
An uma.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.780
No. UMA!

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.610
Unidentified Mysterious Animal!

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.000
Oh, come on. Everyone knows that.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.200
Aw, that's all occult stuff.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.350
Also, at the end of the
Kamakura shogunate,

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:32.080
there was a type of Song period Confucianism,
based on the writings of Zhu Xi.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.230
<b>Want to ask Abe for help?</b>

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.620
This philosophy, also called
"Neo-Confucianism,"

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.930
espoused a theory of justification
by moral law,

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.530
<b>With what?</b>

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.850
specifying a system of ethical and behavioral
standards by which the nobility should live.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:48.680
It became a major philosophical underpinning of
the Kamakura-era anti-shogunate movement.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.250
<b>Kozue.</b>

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.540
<b>Why Abe?</b>

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.270
Make sure to remember this part.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.250
<b>I guess 'cause he's our teacher.</b>

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.710
We're in the middle of class.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.150
I'm sorry.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.320
You too, Kumashiro.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.380
What's going on with those two?

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.480
Naruse?

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.200
What's wrong with Kozue?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.020
Since that NDE experiment yesterday,
she's been like a different person.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.180
I've heard that near-death experiences
can cause people

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.060
to experience personality changes
or recover from health problems.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.560
This is way beyond that.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.690
That's not Kozue.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:40.320
Kozue's got the memory of a cat, but she wouldn't
forget the occult in a million years.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:40.940
A cat?

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.270
All right!

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:44.700
Sorry.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.150
What were you doing?

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.180
If she's forgotten, I'll help her remember.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.410
Help me, Maya.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.420
And so...

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.290
It's a poltergeist!

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.670
Ami-san's just shaking her desk.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.420
A-At last you've revealed yourself, alien!

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.830
You're trying to communicate with the
mother ship, aren't you? Damn it!

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.500
That's not fair, you two.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.680
His handwriting is just really bad.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.870
No way! It won't fit!

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.110
It's okay.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.520
Just slide it in slowly...

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.820
Stop it! Don't be mean to Mr. Snake!

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.360
That's not even worth trying.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.790
Wait, what do you mean?

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:40.310
Aw... I figured all we had to do was hit her with
something occult, and she'd come back.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.790
That's...

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.220
I still haven't returned it.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.300
<i>What's important is what
can't be seen.</i>

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.750
<i>It can be found in a single rose</i>

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.440
<i>or a small bit of water.</i>

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.730
<i>But you can't see it with your eyes.</i>

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.500
<i>You need to see with your heart.</i>

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:10.410
<i>I guess my heart just isn't there yet.
That's why I can't find it.</i>

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.680
<i>But I'll do my best, and someday...</i>

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.390
<i>Someday... Someday...</i>

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.990
<i>My glasses... My glasses...
My glasses...</i>

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.160
No way.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.600
Mikaze-san?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.810
It's something new I'm going to
try selling at the school.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:40.200
You promised to try it, right?

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.400
Yeah, but curry bread right
after eating curry...

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.860
It's not... It's not okay, is it?

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.450
No! I'll eat it! I'll eat it now!

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.380
It's good!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.500
Great!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.760
Actually I have all these left.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.810
I ate too much.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.890
I need to walk around for a bit...

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.030
Wait! Wait!

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:28.860
It's me, Maya!

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.110
Don't use my first name.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.040
What do you want?

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:36.060
I was thinking that the two of us could
talk over the simulators...

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.020
Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:40.850
It's Naruse.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:42.390
What happened with Naruse?

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:43.190
Kozue?

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:46.700
Yeah. Those notes you were
passing with Kuroki...

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.750
Something about asking me about Naruse?

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.500
You suck, reading someone's notes!

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.310
And you shouldn't pass notes in class...

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.460
She really hung up!

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.260
Damn it!

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.190
Oh, crap!

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:18.440
It's ringing!

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.060
It's ringing-

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:19.910
Ow...

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:25.130
Why won't you answer?

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:33.960
Thank you all for gathering here,
on this splendid day, to witness...

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:37.310
Enough talk. Do it.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:38.910
Hey, Maya.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.490
What's he going to do?

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:41.520
You'll see in a second.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.270
Damn you, Maya!

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:49.150
Bend a spoon in front of Naruse?

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:52.090
No matter how much you suck,
you're still Uchida Bunmei, right?

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:53.610
It's Fumiaki.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:57.150
But my ability is...

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.350
Long gone.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:04.090
But still, you clung to your former fame
and learned how to fake doing it.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:04.890
Right?

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:05.570
You know-

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.170
Bend the spoon!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.500
For Kozue.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.090
Principal's orders!

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.390
Orders!

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.550
Orders... Orders...

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:17.010
How the hell does this help Naruse?

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:24.830
What you see here is an ordinary spoon.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:27.770
Nothing special, just a spoon.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:32.630
I'm going to use my psychic
powers to bend it.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:36.250
Hey, you're like Bunmei-kun.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:38.720
Psychic powers? More occult?

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.700
Aw, come on. It looks fun!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.410
Behold!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.600
Ow!

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:14.150
Aw, it's fake.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.930
Of course it is.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.950
There's no such thing as psychic powers.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:23.530
The occult is just lies.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.150
Yes. It's all lies.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:34.670
Psychic powers, UFOs, monsters,
UMAs, OOPArts... It's all lies.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.380
That's proof, right there.

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:40.800
What was it, again?

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.720
"What's important are the things
you can't see with your eyes."

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:45.060
<i>The Little Prince</i>!

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.180
That's all lies, too.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:50.100
Looking with your heart
for what you can't see.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.970
Sure it is.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:58.200
There's nothing you can
see with your heart.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.740
"What's really important
is right beside you."

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.700
"Search with your heart."

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.980
It's all kids stuff.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:07.210
Just like the occult.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.290
Everyone's so obsessed with it. It's silly!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:17.990
Kozue?

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.130
What's wrong with me?

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.950
I'm sorry.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.470
I'm not sad or anything...

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:25.740
I'm so embarrassed.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.270
Kozue!

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.120
She left her heart in the afterlife?!

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:47.490
Her occult-loving heart, to be precise.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:49.180
But that's just a theory.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:51.040
You saw it, too, right?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.560
After the experiment.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.630
But the teacher said that it was
time-lag in the instruments.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.500
Can you explain what we're
seeing any other way?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:04.730
The way she makes fun of the occult,
of <i>The Little Prince</i>...

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.680
And then cries at herself.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.760
That's why you asked Abe?

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.500
That aside...

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:17.030
Right now, Kozue is only half herself.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:22.990
Then we have to go.
Don't we, principal?

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.580
To bring back Kozue's heart.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.950
To the afterlife!

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:37.970
A near-death experience?

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:38.680
Sounds fun.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.840
I'll do it!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.850
It's not a game, JK.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.630
We're bringing back Kozue's heart.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.220
Will you help us, too, Smile?

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.290
A nine-piece hexagon wrench set.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.670
The latest model of riding glove.

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.420
Five liters of engine oil.

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.940
So what's going on?

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:04.410
The key to the laboratory?

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.780
I just want to peek inside.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.800
Is this part of your class?

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.160
Or a private reason?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.650
I suppose the latter.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.160
It's in the top drawer, right?

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:17.420
Give it to me now.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:23.720
Students aren't allowed into the
laboratory for private reasons!

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.060
That was close.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:31.360
Yeah.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.110
She's strangely good at finding things.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:39.770
I can't have her seeing this.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:52.990
"I am a glass shoe, the sign of first
young love, left behind at a ball."

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.830
"Quickly, find the other shoe!"

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:01.450
"The key that will open your heart's door..."

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:08.050
"When the two shoes are together,
we will become one."

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.270
Should I go, too?

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.550
There's only one extra capsule.

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:15.440
It's okay.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:16.860
I'll bring Kozue back.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.770
What do you mean, bring her back?

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.770
Naruse's right there.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.530
You were stalking us,
weren't you? Coward!

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:31.240
Hey... After that embarrassing stunt with
the spoon, I don't want to hear it!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.890
My foot hurt a lot!

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:33.810
I'm the vic-

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.590
Now, now... Come on, you two.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.080
Abe-sensei, there's a reason for this.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.320
Naruse's heart is still in the afterlife?

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.140
To bring her back to normal,

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.380
we need to go into the
afterlife and find her.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.840
Got it? Don't interfere!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:51.140
Wait. It's too dangerous!

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.920
What if the same thing happens
to you as to Naruse?

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.660
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:56.720
It does!

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:58.250
I'm your teacher.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.730
I can't leave Kozue!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.170
Fine.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.280
I'll go.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.750
Okay, going!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.110
The time limit is three minutes.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:21.210
Any more, and reviving you
becomes dangerous.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.890
I don't care what happens to you,
but bring back Kozue.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:26.460
Hey-

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.200
Where am I?

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:54.600
Bunmei-kun!

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:02.130
That's the old me...

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.730
Mom...

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.430
That's Bunmei-kun?

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.510
It's not like it was with Kozue.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:24.780
It doesn't look broken.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:26.150
The instruments are normal.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.900
Then this is what Abe's seeing?

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.170
Probably. There are all types of NDEs.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:33.280
But why?

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:35.710
His life's flashing before him.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:37.340
This is Bunmei's past?

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.670
Hey, Bunmei!

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:41.660
It's Fumiaki.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:42.800
You free tonight?

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.590
Toshi's place has a telescope!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.490
Let's watch the meteor shower!

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:49.210
Meteor shower?

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.200
I remember.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.570
I wanted to see that meteor shower.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.960
Oh, yeah... You're busy, aren't you?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.440
Next time, then.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.220
See you around.

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:03.950
Bye-bye!

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.360
Bye-bye!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.090
You're special.

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:13.330
Don't play with them anymore.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.440
What do you say?

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.290
Yes.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.280
You see the meteor shower?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:24.090
I did! I did!

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.390
It was great!

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:27.190
I made ten wishes!

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.530
It was so amazing!

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.440
Yeah, there were so many.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:36.100
You could see it ten times as
big on Toshi's telescope!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.570
It was so... amazing!

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:46.510
Yes. Sadly, we're booked until next month.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.110
A lecture?

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.320
For graduation ceremonies?

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.200
I'm honored.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.480
That would be in the morning, yes?

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:56.160
The third Wednesday, in the morning...

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.160
Mom, that's...

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.550
Wonderful, it's open.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:00.870
- Mom!
- Yes!

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:01.730
Yes.

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.630
Mom! Mom!

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:06.160
Stop it!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.870
Enough, Fumiaki!

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:24.410
But that day...

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.460
That day is...

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:35.300
That's the day you'd promised to
take me to the planetarium.

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:37.350
Mom...

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.350
What's this?

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:49.880
A movie?

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:00.510
Is Abe nuts or something?

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.640
This is too real.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.590
Maybe it is broken.

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:05.300
This is bad.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.280
It's bad here, too!

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.800
Bunmei, hurry!

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:34.710
Naruse!

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.260
Naruse!

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.280
We're going home, Naruse.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.720
We're running out of time.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:42.660
Naruse, there's no time to explain.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:43.510
Come back with me!

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:46.640
Naruse!

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:47.770
Kozue!

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.270
What are you doing, Kozue?

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.470
Hurry!

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:53.120
It's no good.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:54.560
What isn't?

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.520
What's important can't be
seen with your eyes.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.980
You need to see with your heart.

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:01.960
I still can't...

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.310
Isn't this it?

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:04.830
You've seen plenty!

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.550
I...

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.980
I can't see it.

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:12.770
Naruse...

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:18.170
Is this what you're talking about?

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:35.020
What's really important is right beside you!

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:37.370
That's what it was?

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.220
Her heart had nothing to do with it!

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:44.560
Everyone!

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.920
My near-death experience was awesome!

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.540
It was all sparkly and fluffy!

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:52.200
Aw, you...

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.040
Ow!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.040
I missed you!

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.260
My glasses! My glasses!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.020
Bunmei.

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:15.740
Thank you for saving Kozue.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.780
I'm her teacher.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.300
Fumiaki...

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:23.910
You really were Uchida Fumiaki.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:30.810
Yeah. That was the real Uchida Fumiaki.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:40.740
Soon, Nostradamus's prophecy will come true,
and aliens will invade the Earth.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:44.540
Yeah. Stopping that is my...

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:45.760
Our duty!

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:56.000
Nostradamus's Key.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.740
We need to find it.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:05.560
If we do, you'll be able to
see the meteor shower.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.020
Yeah.

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:18.600
Thank you, Maya.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:21.000
Don't use my first name.

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:36.020
Okay, one croquette bread.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:36.920
Thank you!

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.030
See you again.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.340
Principal!

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:45.040
Thank you so much for letting me sell here!

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:46.500
Nice to meet you.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:48.190
I'm Nakagawa Mikaze.

00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:50.370
Nice to meet you.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.320
Um, are you sure it's okay
to leave your shop...

00:21:57.260 --> 00:21:59.350
Okay, line up!

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:00.590
Next?

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:08.020
Don't do other jobs when you're on duty!

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:53.320
I can't believe it. Everything Bunmei said was true,
and he was a lonely child, just like me.

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:56.260
From now on, we'll work together
and stop the aliens.

00:23:56.260 --> 00:23:58.070
Maya-san, it's a mystery circle!

00:23:58.070 --> 00:23:58.770
Where?

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.060
There are aliens there?

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:01.040
Where?

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.540
What's truly important can only
be seen with your heart!

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:05.500
Mr. Alien!

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.680
She forgot to put her glasses on again.

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:09.960
Next time on <i>Occult Academy</i>:

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:10.960
MAYA's amigo.

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:14.750
I-It's not that I like the occult now, okay?

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.920
This program is a work of fiction.
Departed spirits, psychic abilities,
aliens, UMAs, etc., do not exist.

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:19.920
Unless you believe in them...
